#! /usr/bin/env python3
"""SAT_baseline_py — Python port of the gmtsar C binary SAT_baseline.

Computes the perpendicular / parallel baseline between a reference
(master) and a secondary (aligned) SAR acquisition using their orbit
LED files. Used in the `p2p_processing` pipeline to populate alignment
PRMs before xcorr.

Algorithm (mirrors SAT_baseline.c line-for-line):
  1. Parse both PRMs and their LED files.
  2. For the MASTER orbit, compute the start/center/end ECEF positions
     at radar times t11, t13, t12.
  3. Pre-sample the SECONDARY orbit on a uniform grid spanning the
     acquisition window (±50% / ±200% padding depending on platform).
  4. For each of (t11, t12, t13), grid-walk the secondary orbit to find
     the int-index of the closest-approach sample.
  5. Polyfit-refine (when |t11 - t21| > 10 s) by sampling the secondary
     orbit 100 times in a ±0.005 s window and fitting a 2nd-order poly
     to range², extracting the vertex.
  6. Compute baseline_start/center/end, alpha (degrees from horizontal),
     bpara/bperp via find_parallel_perp_baseline.
  7. Approximate (rshift, ashift) by shooting a look vector from the
     master orbit at near_range and projecting back through llt2rat_sub
     on both PRMs.
  8. Print results in C printf format (PRM key=value lines).

Checkpoints (mirrors Mira #2 ancestor SAT_llt2rat_py):
  B1. PRM/LED parse + ECEF helpers (reused from SAT_llt2rat_py).
  B2. find_unit_vectors / cross3 / get_sign / find_alpha_degrees
      / xyz2plh / find_dist (NEW — small vector geometry).
  B3. calc_height_velocity (NEW — orbital height/velocity calc).
  B4. find_parallel_perp_baseline (NEW — incidence geometry).
  B5. poly_interp (NEW — 100-sample polyfit refinement; reuses
      hermite_orbit + polyfit_c from SAT_llt2rat_py).
  B6. llt2rat_sub (NEW — light recompute of (range, azi) pixels;
      reuses goldop_batch from SAT_llt2rat_py).
  B7. baseline() driver (NEW — main entry point).
  B8. CLI + write_prm_baseline output formatting.

Constants (Mira #2 sub-ULP traps inherited):
  - SOL = 299792456.0 m/s (C #define SOL, gmtsar.h:16)
  - π for plh2xyz/xyz2plh: TRUNCATED 14-digit 3.14159265358979
    (llt2xyz.h:61) — handled by reusing SAT_llt2rat_py's plh2xyz.
  - π for find_parallel_perp_baseline / find_alpha_degrees:
    FULL M_PI = 3.14159265358979323846 (gmtsar.h:13).
    BOTH constants are in play in this binary — DO NOT unify.
  - (1-FL)*(1-FL) ≠ 1-e2 (1 ULP) — handled by plh2xyz reuse.

CLI:
    SAT_baseline_py PRM_master PRM_aligned

Output: PRM-key=value lines on stdout, matching `SAT_baseline`
printf format exactly (trailing spaces, %.12f precision, %d for
shifts).
"""
